Not that I know anything about physics, but isn't Schroedinger's thought
something completely different from Heisenberg's Unschärferelation? The
former is AFAIK about superposition states collapsing by measurement, the
latter about the impossibility to measure location and velocity to an
arbitrary precision (and only for quantum scales not macroscopic scales).
